{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Far be it from me, etc.</b> Meaning: if HaShem has found iniquity for you, I will not rule over the matter but only over what has been revealed to me from the just judgment, and for this sin I judge: ״הָאִישׁ אֲשֶׁר נִמְצָא וְגוֹ׳ יִהְיֶה לִי עָבֶד וְגוֹ׳ וְאַתֶּם עֲלוּ לְשָׁלוֹם״. And with this my mind is at rest regarding what appeared to me difficult — that he spoke, [namely,] that Judah spoke as these words, for this tells that his words were all words of appeasement and he accepted the judgment — and how then, in the very midst of speaking, ״וַיִּגַּשׁ אֵלָיו״ and he spoke words so ancient [i.e., mighty]. But according to our words, the matter is justified, for at first he thought that the matter had gone out from HaShem, that the Elohim had found their iniquity; and when they saw that Joseph accepted only Benjamin alone, he said: this is a sign for you that they were not seized on account of iniquity, and from now on the matter stood on the side of free choice; therefore ״וַיִּגַּשׁ אֵלָיו יְהוּדָה״." "<b>Thus concludes the portion of Mikeitz.</b>"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:48:33.154305019Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}